<title>USA: RTRS-Kennecott talks resume Oct 14.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Kennecott talks resume Oct 14.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor negotiations at Kennecott Copper in Utah have been suspended and will resume October 14, but employees will continue working under terms of the old contract until a new agreement is reached, Kennecott's spokeswoman Alexis Fernandez said.</p>
<p>&quot;They have reached an understanding on the majority of the contract language and we offered a package which we believe is the best in the industry,&quot; Fernandez said. &quot;But it looks like some economic and other issues need more discussion.&quot;</p>
<p>The unions, led by the United Steelworkers of America, negotiated into the early hours of Tuesday morning, past the midnight deadline when the previous three-year contract expired.</p>
<p>USWA officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Some 1,800 employees at the 310,000 short tons per year smelter are represented by labor unions at Kennecott, a subsidiary of Britain's RTZ Plc.</p>
<p>-- Huw Jones, New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
